\title{Generators of classes built by constructor functions}
\description{
Some upstream classes only preset the arguments of their parent class, and
manimR builds them with a function. They still have a class generator, a
subclass of the upstream parent: \code{MathTableClass} inherits from
\code{TableClass}, \code{ReplacementTransformClass} from \code{TransformClass}, and so
on. \code{MathTable()} creates an object of \code{MathTableClass}, so
\code{inherits(x, "MathTable")} is \code{TRUE}, a scene can subclass the generator,
and \code{\link[=set_default]{set_default()}} changes the defaults of that class alone.
}
